# CITATION.cff — prepared at Gate 4 (v0.3.0), not yet released.
# Pending maintainer decisions before release (PROJECT_STATUS.md §6.1):
#   - licence (D4): on approval add
#       license:
#         - MIT          # original code
#         - CC-BY-4.0    # original data and text; third-party material excluded
#   - date-released: add the release date when v0.3.0 is tagged.
#   - doi: add only if a DOI is minted with authorisation.
# The plain citation (SPEC.md §8.3) is valid without a DOI.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or cite the Atlas, please cite it as below. Third-party figures, geometry and quotations keep their own licences and credits, shown next to them in the Atlas."
title: "Spatial Intelligence Atlas — Research Explorer"
version: "0.3.0"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Karahrodi
    given-names: Soroush
repository-code: "https://github.com/soroushkarahrodi79-oss/spatial-intelligence-atlas"
url: "https://soroushkarahrodi79-oss.github.io/spatial-intelligence-atlas/"
abstract: >-
  A static, client-side research explorer for a selected set of geospatial and
  tourism research items. For each item it shows what was asked, where the work
  is situated, how it was done, what evidence is documented, what result was
  reached, what it does not establish, and where the reader can verify it. It
  renders a fixed, hand-authored, source-pinned dataset and performs no live
  analysis, prediction, ranking or scientific validation.
keywords:
  - research explorer
  - evidence
  - geospatial research
  - tourism research
  - reproducibility
